⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the PR's own new test file fails the repo's format gate on the pushed head**

`dart format --set-exit-if-changed` flags `test/providers/stream_trace_io_test.dart` (the rework's BLOCKING-pin test, `e185d9e354`): the test title line is 85 columns over the 80-col budget, so the formatter wants it wrapped:

```dart
// current (85 cols — dart format would change it):
    test('creates a missing parent directory — fresh installs record the trail', () {

// formatter-expected shape:
    test(
      'creates a missing parent directory — fresh installs record the trail',
      () {
        ...
      },
    );
```

Two facts size this finding:

1. It cannot turn validation CI red — the CI static leg is `dart analyze --fatal-infos --fatal-warnings` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:794`, verified green locally on this head); formatting is enforced by the staged-file pre-commit hook (`scripts/pre-commit:41`), which will fail/self-heal the next time anyone touches this file.
2. It contradicts the rework round's posted verification ("`dart format --set-exit-if-changed` over the touched files: **0 changed**") — on the pushed head it is 1 changed. One reformat-and-amend fixes it.

Scope note: my format pass also flags one block in `lib/src/cli/agent_cli.dart` (~line 2467, the `_cli.config.modelsConfig?.overrides` cascade) — that is main-side content outside this PR's diff (pre-existing, main is green), so it is not held against this PR; mentioning it only so a future whole-tree format sweep isn't a surprise.

